<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="00f1317c-9e17-420e-ac39-f25b47295b4b" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--Q2-->
  <exercise data-content-id="eb973c60-4a19-4cee-8d55-46c103eaa674" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="1" data-solution="The actual fish at 2 years old is about 8 mm longer than the linear model estimates." data-solution-options="[&quot;The actual fish at 2 years old is about 8 mm longer than the linear model estimates.&quot;, &quot;The actual fish at 2 years old is about 8 mm shorter than the linear model estimates.&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>7. In the scatter plot below, the length of fish and the age of the fish are shown. The residual for the fish that is 2 years old and 100 mm long is 8.06 mm.
      </para>
      <para><figure><media alt="A SCATTER PLOT THAT SHOWS AGE OF FISH IN YEARS ON THE X-AXIS AND LENGTH OF FISH IN MILLIMETERS ON THE Y-AXIS. A LINE OF BEST FIT IS DRAWN, AND THE POINT (2, 100) IS LABELED."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/4dba1d5b7be716b526731c6ef2dd13a3bc69a934"/></media></figure></para>
      <para>What does this residual mean?</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The actual fish at 2 years old is about 8 mm longer than the linear model estimates.
      </para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 3.3.2 – 3.3.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Do not edit below line.-->
  <solution>
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
